            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-5450",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "glibc: glibc: Heap Buffer Overflow in `scanf` with `%mc` format specifier and large width"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling the scanf family of functions with a %mc (malloc'd character match) in the GNU C Library version 2.7 to version 2.43 with a format width specifier with an explicit width greater than 1024 could result in a one byte heap buffer overflow."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5450",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-5450\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: locales\nFixed Version: 2.35-0ubuntu3.14\nLink: [CVE-2026-5450](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5450)\nCalling the scanf family of functions with a %mc (malloc'd character match) in the GNU C Library version 2.7 to version 2.43 with a format width specifier with an explicit width greater than 1024 could result in a one byte heap buffer overflow.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-5450**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|locales|2.35-0ubuntu3.14|[CVE-2026-5450](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5450)|\n\nCalling the scanf family of functions with a %mc (malloc'd character match) in the GNU C Library version 2.7 to version 2.43 with a format width specifier with an explicit width greater than 1024 could result in a one byte heap buffer overflow."
              },
              "properties": {
