            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-58471",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "wget: GNU Wget: Heap buffer overflow via server-supplied filename leads to memory corruption"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit c2640fe, contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the convert_fname() function within src/url.c that allows remote attackers to trigger memory corruption through a server-supplied filename requiring character set conversion. When the output buffer is too small during iconv E2BIG reallocation, the reallocation logic miscalculates the remaining space, leading to a heap buffer overflow that can be exploited via a maliciously crafted server response."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-58471",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-58471\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: wget\nFixed Version: 1.21.2-2ubuntu1.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-58471](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-58471)\nGNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit c2640fe, contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the convert_fname() function within src/url.c that allows remote attackers to trigger memory corruption through a server-supplied filename requiring character set conversion. When the output buffer is too small during iconv E2BIG reallocation, the reallocation logic miscalculates the remaining space, leading to a heap buffer overflow that can be exploited via a maliciously crafted server response.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-58471**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|wget|1.21.2-2ubuntu1.3|[CVE-2026-58471](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-58471)|\n\nGNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit c2640fe, contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the convert_fname() function within src/url.c that allows remote attackers to trigger memory corruption through a server-supplied filename requiring character set conversion. When the output buffer is too small during iconv E2BIG reallocation, the reallocation logic miscalculates the remaining space, leading to a heap buffer overflow that can be exploited via a maliciously crafted server response."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-58472",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "wget: GNU Wget: Arbitrary code execution or denial of service via crafted HTML attribute"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit dd692d9, contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the html_quote_string() function in src/convert.c that allows a remote attacker to trigger memory corruption by supplying a crafted HTML attribute with a large number of characters requiring entity encoding. A server-supplied HTML attribute causes a signed integer counter to overflow during output size accumulation, resulting in an undersized heap allocation and subsequent heap buffer overflow during the copy phase."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-58472",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-58472\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: wget\nFixed Version: 1.21.2-2ubuntu1.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-58472](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-58472)\nGNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit dd692d9, contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the html_quote_string() function in src/convert.c that allows a remote attacker to trigger memory corruption by supplying a crafted HTML attribute with a large number of characters requiring entity encoding. A server-supplied HTML attribute causes a signed integer counter to overflow during output size accumulation, resulting in an undersized heap allocation and subsequent heap buffer overflow during the copy phase.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-58472**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|wget|1.21.2-2ubuntu1.3|[CVE-2026-58472](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-58472)|\n\nGNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit dd692d9, contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the html_quote_string() function in src/convert.c that allows a remote attacker to trigger memory corruption by supplying a crafted HTML attribute with a large number of characters requiring entity encoding. A server-supplied HTML attribute causes a signed integer counter to overflow during output size accumulation, resulting in an undersized heap allocation and subsequent heap buffer overflow during the copy phase."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.72.0"
        }
